      "name": "Nitesh Sureka",
      "created_at": "2025-08-27T04:33:11.622Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Problem statement :<br>\nWhen we give an advance to a creditor, right now it goes to the creditor account.<br>\nI want the amount to go to the advance to creditors account and at the time of raising the invoice this advance could be adjusted with the Invoice.</p>\n<p>Existing Solution :<br>\nThis happens in ERP Next at the moment but the advances go to the Creditor account as a debit balance, which we dont want, we need it in advances.<br>\nIn the supplier master, there is a field where we can tag an advance account. But I guess that’s not working properly.</p>\n<p>Help :<br>\nIs there any other way through which we can handle this in ERPNext? Also, when we book an invoice against this particular supplier, the advances should be fetched automatically. Can somebody please guide and help?</p>",
